{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And his rock, etc.</b> His rock shall pass away, that is, the boundary of his kingdom, out of the greatness of his fear. And this is the meaning of ממגור. And the sense is: he shall flee and not lean upon his rock, [and his dismay] from every banner that his princes see — whether those who flee or those who remain in his land." "<b>A fire and a furnace.</b> An allusion to the altar, or by way of parable, as he mentioned above: 'and a flame of fire that consumes.'"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {0 "Reading [וחתו] as 'and his dismay/shattering'; the word is textually uncertain and may be corrupt."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:16.587966056Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}